@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Trade-time Market evidence — build 2240
+
+Baseline production/current clean main: v1.22.24/build2239, b982e49ded18455e2fcc4fab58610569cc784343, tree0ca79a715f697147c8081d4d69f1afd7efca9bb4. Public readiness and Render deployment metadata agree. No related unfinished PR exists. The next tag/release v1.22.25 was unused before edits.
+
+## Real coverage and authority
+
+Reuse the prior audit at c48d4a9fb96420c2aae397535d08b68dd1a461d9/.task-evidence/trade-time-market-coverage-2239. Its 25-trade replay has no paired real Market population and is not production-zero evidence. Main Chat subsequently supplied an authorized Render-local bounded screen: at least one qualifying pre-trade quote for10/26DayTraders events and3/11Arkham events, none of31sampledGranite events. These are event counts from retained trade-execution references, not exhaustive coverage, asset counts, package completeness, historical format parity or a Codex-reproduced private snapshot. No private payload or credentials are copied. Seven days is only a screening bucket, never an expiry threshold.
+
+The useful authorized scope is individual retained quotes. No package totals are added to the interface. The disclosure explicitly withholds whole-package comparison until complete real coverage, compatible historical league format and a documented package freshness policy are substantiated. Older individual observations remain labeled dated estimates with visible age. Existing model calculations and retained grades are not rewritten; a canonical technical completeness check does not certify package freshness or decision quality.
+
+## Matched failure and correction
+
+On an exact production-source checkout, two new matched controls fail: a newer incompatible quote masks an older compatible quote, as does a newer foreign-league quote. Both fail assertions, without setup errors. Shared sparse selection now accepts an optional pure admission predicate before selecting a winner. Other callers retain their existing default temporal contract. Trade supplies the extracted existing exact identity/units/format/method and scope checks plus explicit unknown/later knowledge/publication protection. Unknown metadata stays unavailable.
+
+Selection streams only the exact asset and one or two existing asset-type contexts, keeps constant candidate state and acquires no lifecycle lease. Picks consider both supported aliases in one query; conflicting same-instant prices are withheld rather than arbitrarily selected by ID. No provider resolver, pricing formula, store schema, source acquisition or permanent storage is added. Exact picks never borrow a converted player's quote. Rejected foreign-scope records are not rendered as raw evidence.
+
+The existing quote card leads with the value, exact-observation/dated-estimate label, source, observation date, age and missing-value reason. Age uses the oldest admitted provider observation, not a later attachment/retrieval or grading timestamp. Subsecond ages do not claim the trade instant. Technical format, provenance and excluded evidence remain under the existing disclosure. No new page-render solver, background search or provider work.
+
+## Validation boundaries
+
+Focused tests cover newer-incompatible/foreign masking, exact pick aliases and conflicts, partial/stale/zero/subsecond values, later or ambiguous knowledge, publication clocks, missing metadata, conversion and no durable growth. Phone controls use actual existing routes at320×432,375×667,390×844,1280×900 with keyboard, touch emulation, source/age, no overflow and no disclosure requests. Existing History chain/contextual Back/pagination/Forward/reload and league isolation are preserved. Fixtures are not real coverage, live acceptance or physical Safari acceptance.
+
+First focused execution had four new-fixture assertion failures: equivalent UTC spelling and cross-fixture reuse of the process-wide history cache. Disposable cache isolation and canonical timestamp comparison corrected those fixture assumptions without weakening the original values/assertions. The expanded controls passed162tests before final metadata/commit. A later lint pass identified one unused import and three single-line test statements; those were corrected. Original logs remain separate. Final exact-source full/canonical/hosted results and manifests are required for release; this source note does not claim they have already passed.
+
+Validation scratch recovery losslessly archives old standalone validation copies, verifies every readable byte and preserves inaccessible originals unchanged. Original tool-method failures are retained; no permission escalation, current source loss, production eviction, cache clear, infrastructure change or scratch-prerequisite reduction is authorized.
+
+## Live acceptance
+
+This session has management/public HTTP access but no attached authenticated owner browser or Render Shell executor. The prior unchanged external401is not retried. Main Chat's supplied Render-local evidence is authoritative supplied evidence, not reproduced by Codex. Post-deployment public readiness/assets and auth-boundary checks remain distinct from private per-asset acceptance. Do not force entry/sync, rebuild FOIS, search trades or change preferences to demonstrate this feature. Trade256+128MiB, FOIS768MiB, restoration16× and the2GiBcap remain unchanged.
